          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઓછાબોલું (ochābolũ) is built from ઓછું (ochũ), \"less\", and the stem of બોલવું (bolvũ), \"to speak\": someone who speaks little. CDIAL lists Gujarati ochũ under ōccha- (CDIAL 2540) and bolvũ under bōll- (CDIAL 9321)."
            }
          ]
        },
